On Wed, Oct 6, 2010 at 3:56 PM, Luke Bergen <lukeabergen@gmail.com> wrote:
> I think what ruler11 is getting at (and I've also started similar
> discussions with little success) is... "let's talk about things that you
> would say in lojban when a jerk cuts you off in rush hour traffic".

The odds that they would understand what you say are slim, so you
could just say "mi klama le zarci" or "doi sfofa" with a suitably
angry tone and they will probably get the message.

If you suspect they might actually be a Lojbanist, you could go with a mild:

    ko setca lo stedu be do lo ganxo be lo xarju

or if you want to get really nasty:

    .a'o do bai lifri lo cnino gismu ca ro djedi pe lo nu do jmive
    "May a new gismu be inflicted upon you every day of your life"

or something. Just be creative.

mu'o mi'e xorxes

